article: Plain Text Forever
author: Jordan Parker
drafted: 2025-02-01
published: 2025-02-14


  Why I keep my writing in plain text, and a tour of the inline styles
  that Articles supports.

Inline Styles

  You can write **bold**, *italic*, __also bold__, _also italic_,
  ~~strikethrough~~, and `inline code`. A link looks like
  [the Articles repo](https://github.com/nepthar/articles). Underscores in
  a word like snake_case_name stay as they are. So does math like 2 * 3 * 4.

Blocks

  A block with no directive keeps its line breaks:

    Roses are plain text,
    violets are too,
    nothing to render,
    nothing to do.

  A code block keeps its text exactly. Inline styles do not apply here:

    code: python
    def area(w, h):
        return w*h*1  # the *s stay as written

  A quote:

    quote: Somebody Wise
    Plain text outlives every format
    that tried to replace it.


The Long View

  This section comes after a major section break (two empty lines), so it
  is a major section.
